PROBLEM STATEMENT:
Given an integer array nums sorted in non-decreasing order, square every element and return a new array containing the squares in non-decreasing order.
For example:
[-4, -1, 0, 3, 10]
After squaring:
[16, 1, 0, 9, 100]
After sorting:
[0, 1, 9, 16, 100]
AIM:
To square every element of a sorted array and return the squared values in sorted order
JAVA CODE:
class Solution {
    public int[] sortedSquares(int[] nums) {

        int n = nums.length;
        int[] result = new int[n];

        int left = 0;
        int right = n - 1;

        // Fill the result array from the end
        for (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {

            if (Math.abs(nums[left]) > Math.abs(nums[right])) {
                result[i] = nums[left] * nums[left];
                left++;
            } else {
                result[i] = nums[right] * nums[right];
                right--;
            }
        }

        return result;
    }
}
INPUT:
nums = [-4,-1,0,3,10]
OUTPUT:
[0,1,9,16,100]
